sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: restore a host development Instance whose removal failed after its Route withdrawal; no fence settlement, no new publish path.
  %% Tightened: refusals at admission; the run checks the databases, republishes through Route create, then clears this removal's journal rows.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:restore
  %% kind: instance.restore
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Nodes<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:restore 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:restore 42`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:restore <instance> [--json]`
  Note over GW: Check the failed removal
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a host development Instance, not a container, in `removing`
  %%> - its live removal is `failed`, and every removal Operation has ended; a timed-out run without a native end refuses
  %%> - every removal run recorded each planned step that deletes data as skipped: source, Processes, teardown
  %%> - the removal saved no Schedule and no SQLite file
  %%> - its one Route is `retiring` with the same domain and targets
  %%> - the Node agent reports the checkout: same top level, origin of the Project's repository
  %%> - no other Operation holds the Instance or its Route
  alt a check fails
    %% path: refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>instance.restore_*
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; no Operation starts
  else the removal can be undone
    %% path: main
    GW->>SW: Start the restore run<br/>operation-instance-restore
    %%> Captures:
    %%> - the database names the removal planned, per server
    %%> - the Route create plan for the same Route, targets and domain
    %%> - holds the publication Nodes, as Route create does
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the CLI follows the instance.restore Operation
    SW->>N: Check the databases<br/>admin client · read-only
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each planned database exists and accepts connections
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - `instance.restore_database_closed` or `instance.restore_database_missing` names the databases; this command opens nothing
    SW->>N: Republish the Route<br/>operation-route-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the Route create children unchanged: CSR, sign, site, TLS probe
    %%> - writes the awake marker again
    SW->>N: Clear the fence journal<br/>admin client · one transaction
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks again that every planned database is open
    %%> - deletes only the journal rows whose OID and name match a planned database
    alt the run succeeds
      %% path: restored
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
      Note over GW: Record restored<br/>one transaction
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Instance `active`, removal and members `abandoned`, Route `active` and published
      %%> - the destroy Operation keeps its failure
      GW-->>CLI: Instance restored
    else a step fails
      %% path: failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Instance stays `removing`, the removal `failed`, the Route `retiring`
      %%> - a site published before a later failure serves until the next run
      %%> - run `instance:restore` again, or `instance:destroy`
    end
  end
